{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: implement `solve(case)` that filters API calls based on normalized gain threshold.\n\nFrom the payload structure:\n- `threshold`: minimum normalized gain to accept\n- `calls`: list of call objects with:\n  - `call_id`: string\n  - `loss_without_call`: float\n  - `loss_with_call`: float\n  - `prediction_tokens`: int\n  - `parseable`: boolean\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. For each call, compute gain = `loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by `prediction_tokens` (divide by prediction_tokens)\n3. Accept call if `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` and `diagnostics` (in original order)\n\nThe output schema:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain`\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, normalized = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, normalized = 0.37796304 / 4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, normalized = 0.74550131 / 6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, normalized = 0.7595393 / 5 = 0.1519079, parseable=true → accepted (wait, this should be accepted since 0.15 \u003e 0.05)\n\nWait, but the candidate artifact mentions \"normalized_weights, stronger_counterfactual\" - let me re-read.\n\n\"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" - so max(prediction_tokens, 1)?\n\n\"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold\" - inclusive_threshold means `\u003e=`\n\nLet me look at case 002, call4: parseable=false → should NOT be accepted regardless of gain.\n\nThe implementation seems straightforward. Let me also check if \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" means I should round the normalized_gain. The schema says `\"type\": \"number\"` so no specific rounding precision is mentioned, but the artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places, maybe 8 or just leave as float.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, \"rounded\" might just mean I should round to some precision. I'll use round() with maybe 8 decimal places to avoid floating point noise, or just return the raw computed value.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        # Normalize by at least one token\n        denom = max(tokens, 1)\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / denom\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. The response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me format the Python source properly as a JSON string with escaped newlines and proper escaping.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        # Normalize by at least one prediction token (stronger counterfactual, normalized weights)\\n        denom = max(tokens, 1)\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / denom\\n\\n        # Inclusive threshold: accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01maH8OMNFegyaqjtN1i6wZM","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2474,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":45,"output_tokens":1295,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":996},"service_tier":"standard"}}